    <ul>
      <li>Worm spine removed from drive path entirely — it was the single most complex and failure-prone component</li>
      <li>Each cylinder shaft now has a locked differential at its midpoint — couples that shaft's rotation into the amber driveshaft</li>
      <li>Single amber driveshaft passes through all three locked diffs — all three shafts contribute torque into one continuous shaft</li>
      <li>Amber driveshaft exits rear of engine box → CVT hydrostatic transmission (CRV-style) → rear 2WD axle</li>
      <li>CVT gives smooth variable ratio output — no gear steps, no clutch — torque multiplication handled hydraulically</li>
      <li>17.5:1 chain to dual alternators RETAINED: cylinder shaft 1 front exit → helical pinion → chain → 3,500 RPM alternators</li>
      <li>Drive configuration: Phase 20 was 4WD via worm → gearbox → transfer → locked diffs. Phase 21 is rear 2WD via CVT only</li>
      <li>All locomotive rail, piston, wheel, steam, water, and electrical specs unchanged from Phase 20</li>
    </ul>
