<!-- AEGIS BOILER OVERVIEW -->
<div class="panel active" id="panel-aegis">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--aegis)">Diagram 1 · Aegis Boiler Mark 1 — Phase 23</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">Domed Cube SS 304 · Hemispherical Copper Bowl · Dome Rivets · TIG Corner Trim · 90 PSI</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    The Aegis Boiler Mark 1 is named after the Roman curved shield — the dome geometry deflects pressure force into surface tension exactly as a curved shield deflects projectile force into lateral deflection.
    The Phase 23 design replaces the Temple Pyramid concept with a hemispherical copper bowl — simpler to machine on a lathe in a single operation, superior steam escape dynamics, and better counter-flow geometry.
    The bowl sits concave face up inside the domed cube vessel. Water mist falls by gravity from the top center injector into the concave bowl interior. Steam generated at the bowl surface rises naturally upward — counter-flow to the falling water — into the steam collection zone above the bowl rim.
    TIG welded curved trim edges on all interior cube corners eliminate stress concentration points and smooth the pressure flow path around corners, reducing turbulence in the steam collection zone.
    The four outward locomotive domes on the side faces of the cube handle internal pressure through surface tension rather than flat face bending stress — same principle as a locomotive boiler barrel end.
    All steam exits through two high-position standpipe outlets on the front face ensuring only dry steam reaches the pistons.
  </p>

