  <p class="section-lead">
    The Aegis Bowl is a true 90-degree copper hemisphere 10cm in diameter. It sits inside the 12cm inner cavity with exactly 1cm annular gap each side between the bowl rim and the vessel inner wall.
    This 1cm gap on each side equals 20mm total annular clearance — just above the 19mm minimum steam flow spec that runs throughout the entire system matching the 3/4 inch steam pipe diameter.
    The four outward locomotive domes on the vessel side faces add effective interior clearance beyond the nominal 12cm at their widest points, providing additional steam escape path at those four points around the bowl circumference.
    Dome rivets cover the entire concave interior face of the bowl in a uniform hexagonal pattern. All dome rivets are the same size throughout — 5mm diameter dome, 3mm height — for Phase 23 first build ease of machining.
    TIG welded curved fillet trim on all four interior corners of the cube vessel eliminates sharp 90-degree corner edges. Sharp interior corners create stress concentration under pressure cycling and also create turbulent dead zones where steam pressure can build unevenly. The curved fillets smooth both the mechanical stress distribution and the steam flow path.
