<!-- WATER SYSTEM -->
<div class="panel" id="panel-water">
<div class="wrap">
  <div class="eyebrow" style="color:var(--water)">Diagram 3 · Complete Water System — Phase 23</div>
  <h2 class="section-title">10 Gal Poly Tank → Pump → Dual Filter → Check Valve → EWI Mist → Aegis Boiler → Condenser Loop</h2>
  <p class="section-lead">
    Complete water supply chain for Phase 23. The 10 gallon polypropylene unpressurized tank feeds a 24V diaphragm pump which supplies two stages of inline filtration — 50 micron sediment then 5 micron fine — before the high pressure EWI micro pump raises the water to 100–300 PSI. A check valve between the solenoid injector and atomizing nozzle prevents boiler back-pressure entering the EWI system. Water arrives at the Aegis Bowl as high velocity atomized mist. Condenser loop recovers exhaust steam back to liquid and returns it to the tank. Near-zero net water consumption at operating conditions with condenser running. Preferred fill: distilled or deionized water. Emergency fill: clean tap water acceptable — note in service log.
  </p>

