  <div class="warn-box">
    <h4>⚠ Phase 23 Cost and Build Notes</h4>
    <ul>
      <li>Copper bowl replaces pyramid — significant machining cost reduction. Bowl is one lathe operation. Pyramid was three levels of stepped geometry with two rivet types. Estimated savings of $600–900 in machining labour.</li>
      <li>TIG fillet weld on interior corners: specify this to the vessel fabricator when ordering the domed cube. It is a weld finishing operation — not expensive if done while the vessel is still on the bench before assembly.</li>
      <li>Check valve on nozzle: specify 400 PSI water rated — not the 300 PSI EWI operating pressure. You want margin above operating pressure.</li>
      <li>Steam trap: thermostatic type is simplest for this application. Float type also works but has more moving parts. Either is acceptable at 90 PSI and exhaust temperatures.</li>
      <li>Halloween whistle: source a genuine multi-chime steam whistle rated for your pressure. Model train suppliers, steam hobby suppliers, and industrial suppliers all carry these. Budget $120–250 for a quality multi-chime unit.</li>
      <li>Phase 23 total estimate ~$34–38.5K vs Phase 22 ~$36–40.5K — Phase 23 is actually slightly cheaper due to bowl simplification despite adding exhaust system components. Net cost reduction of approximately $2,000.</li>
    </ul>
